# Cursor Rule: LMCS Project – Cahier des Charges (CDC) Context

## Rule Name

lmcs-cdc-context

## Scope

This rule applies to **the entire LMCS Insight repository** (frontend, backend, and any future modules). It encodes the **official project specification** (Cahier des Chargés, Phase II 2025-2026). All design, feature, and terminology decisions must align with this context.

**Do not improvise on domain logic or user roles:** refer to this document.

---

# 1. PROJECT IDENTITY

## 1.1 Official Title

- **French:** Suivi des encadrements des chercheurs du laboratoire LMCS - ESI  
- **English:** Tracking of supervisions of researchers at the LMCS laboratory - ESI  

## 1.2 Project Number & Year

- **N° Projet:** CP_PRJ02 (Projet 2CP)  
- **Année universitaire:** 2025-2026  
- **Phase:** Phase II (2025-2026) of a triennial project (2024-2026).

## 1.3 Institution & Laboratory

- **Laboratoire:** LMCS — Laboratoire des Méthodes de Conception de Systèmes  
- **École:** ESI — École Nationale Supérieure d'Informatique  
- **Mission:** Production and diffusion of scientific knowledge through the work of its researchers.

---

# 2. PROJECT BACKGROUND & MOTIVATION

## 2.1 Phase I (2024-2025) – Already Done

- Centralized **scientific productions database** for LMCS researchers.  
- Phase II must **interconnect** with this existing base (interoperability).

## 2.2 Phase II (2025-2026) – Current Scope

- **Goal:** Extend the system to **track academic and scientific supervisions** carried out by teachers/researchers.  
- **Current pain points:**
  - Supervision data (PFE, Masters, Doctorates, projects, internships, etc.) are **dispersed** (Excel, Word, emails, personal archives).  
  - Data are **not normalized** and **hard to exploit** for reliable reports.  
  - **Consequences:**
    - Difficult to justify pedagogical and scientific activities.  
    - Slow production of statistics requested by direction, school, or evaluation bodies.  
    - Time loss in data collection.  
    - Risk of errors or omissions in reports.  
    - Low visibility of themes actually supervised.  
    - Difficulty linking supervisions to research axes and scientific productions.

## 2.3 Strategic Need

The laboratory needs a **structured, reliable, and evolutive tool** to manage all supervisions in a coherent way and to offer, in the long run, a **global view of laboratory activities** (with Phase I data).

---

# 3. TYPES OF SUPERVISIONS (DOMAIN ENTITIES)

The system must handle **all** of the following. Each is a type of "encadrement":

| Type (FR)              | Type (EN) / Short   | Description / Notes                    |
|------------------------|---------------------|----------------------------------------|
| Projet de Fin d'Études | PFE (engineer)      | End-of-study engineering project       |
| Mémoire de Master      | Master             | Master's thesis                        |
| Thèse de Doctorat      | Doctorate          | PhD thesis                             |
| Stage académique      | SPE / Academic stage| Academic internship                    |
| Projets de recherche   | Research project   | National and international research    |

- Supervisions can be **internal to LMCS** or **external co-supervision**.  
- Both **current** and **past** supervisions must be covered.

---

# 4. USER ROLES (ACTORS)

Exactly **three** main profiles are specified. Implement roles and permissions accordingly.

## 4.1 Direction du laboratoire (Laboratory Director)

- **Responsibilities:**
  - Consult **global statistics**.  
  - Monitor **supervision workload**.  
  - Prepare **annual reports** (bilans annuels).  
- **Implied features:** Read-only dashboards, aggregated stats, export for reports, high-level views.

## 4.2 Enseignants / Chercheurs (Teachers / Researchers)

- **Responsibilities:**
  - **Enter and update** their own supervisions.  
  - **Consult** their supervision history.  
- **Implied features:** CRUD on own supervisions, list/filter own encadrements, possibly limited stats on own data.

## 4.3 Administrateur système (System Administrator)

- **Responsibilities:**
  - **User account management**.  
  - **Validation / moderation** of data if needed.  
  - **Functional maintenance** of the database.  
- **Implied features:** User CRUD, optional validation workflow, backup/restore, admin-only settings.

---

# 5. FUNCTIONAL OBJECTIVES (DETAILED)

## 5.1 Suivi des encadrements (Supervision tracking)

- **Register** all types of supervisions (PFE, Master, Doctorate, stage, research project, etc.).  
- **Associate one or several supervisors** to each work.  
- **Manage co-supervisions** (internal and external).

## 5.2 Gestion des étudiants / doctorants (Students / PhD candidates)

- **Student-related data:**  
  - Name, first name  
  - Institution  
  - Level (niveau)  
  - Speciality (spécialité)  
- **Academic year** (année universitaire).  
- **Progress state (état d'avancement):** e.g. in progress, defended, abandoned, extension, etc.

## 5.3 Suivi thématique (Thematic tracking)

- **Link each supervision to:**
  - A **research theme** (thématique de recherche).  
  - A **team or axis** of the laboratory (équipe ou axe du laboratoire).  
- **Keywords** describing the subject (mots-clés).

## 5.4 Suivi temporel (Temporal tracking)

- **Start date** (date de début).  
- **Planned defense date** (date prévue de soutenance).  
- **Actual defense date** (date réelle de soutenance).

## 5.5 Exploitation statistique (Statistics & analytics)

Analyses must be **multi-criteria**, including by:

- Enseignant/chercheur (teacher/researcher)  
- Année universitaire (academic year)  
- Type d'encadrement (type of supervision)  
- Thématique de recherche (research theme)  
- État d'avancement (progress state)

## 5.6 Aide au bilan du laboratoire (Support for laboratory reports)

The system must support:

- **Number of supervisions per teacher and per period.**  
- **Breakdown by type** (PFE, Master, Doctorate, etc.).  
- **Defense rate** (taux de soutenance).  
- **Thematic distribution** of supervised work.

---

# 6. MINIMAL FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS (MUST-HAVE)

The CDC explicitly lists these as **minimal**:

1. **Gestion des enseignants/chercheurs** — Management of teachers/researchers (e.g. directory, profiles).  
2. **Gestion des étudiants encadrés** — Management of supervised students.  
3. **Gestion des sujets d'encadrement** — Management of supervision subjects (topics, titles, descriptions).  
4. **Affectation des encadrants** — Assignment of supervisors (one or several per supervision).  
5. **Mise à jour de l'état d'avancement** — Updating progress state (in progress, defended, abandoned, etc.).  
6. **Recherche multicritère** — Multicriteria search (filters on type, year, teacher, theme, state, etc.).  
7. **Tableaux de bord et statistiques** — Dashboards and statistics.  
8. **Export des données** — Export (PDF, Excel explicitly cited).

All inputs/outputs (screens, forms, dashboards, reports) are to be defined **in collaboration with LMCS laboratory managers**; the above list is the mandatory baseline.

